# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — Files and directories that Git should NEVER commit.
#
# TERRAFORM-SPECIFIC ENTRIES — Explained why each is excluded:
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL .terraform DIRECTORY
# Contains downloaded provider binaries (.terraform/providers/) and modules.
# These are LARGE (100+ MB) and version-pinned by .terraform.lock.hcl anyway.
# Every team member runs `terraform init` to get their own copy.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.terraform/*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TERRAFORM STATE FILE
# terraform.tfstate contains the ENTIRE state of your infrastructure:
# resource IDs, attributes, and sometimes sensitive values.
# Committing this = exposing infrastructure details + potential secrets.
# It also causes merge conflicts when multiple people run terraform.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TERRAFORM STATE BACKUP
# terraform.tfstate.backup is the PREVIOUS state (auto-created before apply).
# Same sensitivity as the main state file.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tfstate.backup

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TERRAFORM LOCK FILE (controversial — we KEEP it committed)
# .terraform.lock.hcl should actually BE COMMITTED in most projects because
# it ensures identical provider versions across the team. However, some
# teams prefer to .gitignore it and rely on version constraints alone.
# We DO commit it (it's NOT in this .gitignore) for reproducible builds.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRASH LOGS
# crash.log and crash.*.log are generated when Terraform panics.
# They contain stack traces and potentially sensitive data.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
crash.log
crash.*.log

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OVERRIDE FILES
# Files named override.tf or *_override.tf are Terraform's built-in
# override mechanism. They MERGE with existing configuration and are
# typically used for local development overrides. They should never
# be committed — they're personal per-developer.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLI CONFIGURATION
# .terraformrc and terraform.rc are per-user Terraform CLI configuration.
# Contains plugin cache paths, credentials helpers, etc. Personal, not shared.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VARIABLE DEFINITIONS FILE
# terraform.tfvars contains YOUR specific values (key names, region
# preferences, sometimes secrets). It's personal and should never
# be committed. The .example version IS committed as a template.
#
# Also ignore *.auto.tfvars which are auto-loaded variable files.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
# EXCEPTION: Allow the .example file
!*.tfvars.example

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PLAN FILES
# Binary plan files generated by `terraform plan -out=plan.tfplan`.
# These contain a snapshot of the ENTIRE configuration and state —
# including sensitive values. They're also binary and meaningless in git.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tfplan

# =============================================================================
# NON-TERRAFORM ENTRIES
# =============================================================================

# SSH private keys — NEVER commit these!
*.pem
*.ppk
id_rsa*
*.key

# Ansible inventory files (contain IPs)
hosts.ini
hosts

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# Backup files
*.backup
*.bak

keys/